        <briefdescription>
<para>Approximate equality comparator, with an explicit tolerance. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The comparison succeeds if the distance between <computeroutput>lhs</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>rhs</computeroutput> is less than <computeroutput>epsilon</computeroutput>. The operands are numbers, integral or floating-point, possibly of different types, or the framework value wrappers and numeric literals, whose own tolerance is not used. For the integers, the distance is computed exactly, also for operands of different signedness, so <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-literals_1gafe47800a219b00fcccf0a1dc596dbe20" kindref="member">approx</ref> (0u, -1, 2)</computeroutput> succeeds; for the other types, in their common floating-point type. A failure is reported as <computeroutput>lhs ~ (rhs +/- epsilon)</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal">t.expect<sp/>(mt::approx<sp/>(read_adc<sp/>(),<sp/>512,<sp/>3))<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;ADC<sp/>reading&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">t.expect<sp/>(mt::approx<sp/>(compute_float<sp/>(),<sp/>42.0f,<sp/>0.001f));</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>The <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-literals_1gafe47800a219b00fcccf0a1dc596dbe20" kindref="member">approx</ref> (value, epsilon)</computeroutput> form is a value wrapper instead, which applies its tolerance to the six comparisons and to the operators; it accepts only floating-point values.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Lhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type of the left hand side operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Rhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type of the right hand side operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Epsilon_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type of the tolerance.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>lhs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Left hand side operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>rhs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Right hand side operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>epsilon</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The tolerance; a negative one fails all comparisons. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A comparator object that evaluates to true if <computeroutput>lhs</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>rhs</computeroutput> differ by less than <computeroutput>epsilon</computeroutput>.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="since"><para>5.1.0</para>
</simplesect>
The <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-literals_1gafe47800a219b00fcccf0a1dc596dbe20" kindref="member">approx</ref></computeroutput> function template constructs a <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1approx__op" kindref="compound">detail::approx_op</ref></computeroutput> from the forwarded operands and tolerance; the operands are numbers, so <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1a51e86043001b197561806d5c6297041b" kindref="member">detail::as_operand()</ref></computeroutput>, which converts the C strings, is not needed. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
