<simplesect kind="return"><para>A comparator object that evaluates to true if <computeroutput>lhs</computeroutput> is greater than or equal to <computeroutput>rhs</computeroutput>.</para>
</simplesect>
The operands are passed to <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1a51e86043001b197561806d5c6297041b" kindref="member">detail::as_operand()</ref></computeroutput>, as for <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-function-comparators_1gaa7c7b6a7ad32856edc235a05e77d8c7f" kindref="member">eq()</ref></computeroutput>, so that the C strings are compared by content. It constructs a comparator object, with the <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1greater__equal" kindref="compound">detail::greater_equal</ref></computeroutput> tag, which evaluates to <computeroutput>true</computeroutput> if <computeroutput>lhs</computeroutput> is greater than or equal to <computeroutput>rhs</computeroutput>, and which is reported with both values if not. </para>
