    <briefdescription>
<para>Functions for comparing actual and expected values in tests. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>While any boolean expression can be used in expectations and requirements, dedicated comparator functions such as <computeroutput>eq</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>ne</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>lt</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>le</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>gt</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>ge</computeroutput> provide enhanced reporting by explicitly showing the compared values when a check fails.</para>
<para>Using these comparators ensures that failed checks report both actual and expected values, making issues easier to diagnose.</para>
<para>Comparators are available for both fundamental types and standard containers. When a container comparison fails, the elements of both containers are shown.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Examples</title><para></para>
</simplesect>
<programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal">ts.test<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Check<sp/>various<sp/>conditions&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>[]<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal">&amp;<sp/>t)<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::eq<sp/>(compute_answer<sp/>(),<sp/>42))<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;answer<sp/>is<sp/>42&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::ne<sp/>(compute_answer<sp/>(),<sp/>43))<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;answer<sp/>is<sp/>not<sp/>43&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::lt<sp/>(compute_answer<sp/>(),<sp/>43))<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;answer<sp/>is<sp/>&lt;<sp/>43&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::le<sp/>(compute_answer<sp/>(),<sp/>43))<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;answer<sp/>is<sp/>&lt;=<sp/>43&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::gt<sp/>(compute_answer<sp/>(),<sp/>41))<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;answer<sp/>is<sp/>&gt;<sp/>41&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::ge<sp/>(compute_answer<sp/>(),<sp/>42))<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;answer<sp/>is<sp/>&gt;=<sp/>42&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(compute_condition<sp/>())<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;condition<sp/>is<sp/>true&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">});</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>If a comparator check fails, the output clearly indicates the actual and expected values:</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".console"><codeline><highlight class="normal">Check<sp/>failed<sp/>comparisons</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>✗<sp/>actual<sp/>!=<sp/>42<sp/>FAILED<sp/>(unit-test.cpp:286,<sp/>42<sp/>!=<sp/>42)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>✗<sp/>FAILED<sp/>(unit-test.cpp:307,<sp/>42<sp/>!=<sp/>42)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>✗<sp/>(actual<sp/>==<sp/>42)<sp/>and<sp/>(actual<sp/>!=<sp/>42.0)<sp/>FAILED<sp/>(unit-test.cpp:781,<sp/>(42<sp/>==<sp/>42<sp/>and<sp/>42.0<sp/>!=<sp/>42.0))</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>The C strings (<computeroutput>char</computeroutput> arrays, including the string literals, and <computeroutput>char</computeroutput> pointers) are compared by content, also with <computeroutput>std::string</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>std::string_view</computeroutput>, so <computeroutput>mt::eq (actual, "abc")</computeroutput> checks the characters, not the addresses; a null <computeroutput>char</computeroutput> pointer is equal only to another null pointer (or <computeroutput>nullptr</computeroutput>), not to an empty string. The other pointers and arrays (including <computeroutput>uint8_t</computeroutput> buffers) are compared by address.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Comparing Containers</title><para></para>
</simplesect>
Containers can be compared for equality or inequality using the same comparator functions. The comparison is performed with the standard <computeroutput>==</computeroutput> operator, so the containers must be of the same type. The standard <computeroutput>==</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>!=</computeroutput> operators return a plain <computeroutput>bool</computeroutput>, so a failed check could not show the elements.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Examples</title><para></para>
</simplesect>
<programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="keyword">namespace<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal">mt<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus" kindref="compound">micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus</ref>;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">ts.test<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Check<sp/>containers&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>[]<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal">&amp;<sp/>t)<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::eq<sp/>(std::vector&lt;int&gt;{<sp/>1,<sp/>2<sp/>},<sp/>std::vector&lt;int&gt;{<sp/>1,<sp/>2<sp/>}))</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;vector{<sp/>1,<sp/>2<sp/>}<sp/>eq<sp/>vector{<sp/>1,<sp/>2<sp/>}&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::ne<sp/>(std::vector&lt;int&gt;{<sp/>1,<sp/>2,<sp/>3<sp/>},</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>std::vector&lt;int&gt;{<sp/>1,<sp/>2,<sp/>4<sp/>}))</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;vector{<sp/>1,<sp/>2,<sp/>3<sp/>}<sp/>ne<sp/>vector{<sp/>1,<sp/>2,<sp/>4<sp/>}&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">});</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
    </detaileddescription>
  </compounddef>
